    {
      "id": 1,
      "text": "Patrick Springs got its name in 1925 when the post office, train depot, and community were all officially renamed from Shuff to Patrick Springs.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Patrick_Springs%2C_Virginia",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s first post office opened in 1857 as Spabrook Station near the old Patrick Springs hotel and mineral resort.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Patrick_Springs%2C_Virginia",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Reverend Jacob Shough, a Methodist circuit rider, ran a store and post office and built the old Shough grist mill, one of the area’s oldest landmarks.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Patrick_Springs%2C_Virginia",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Shough grist mill operated through four generations of the Shough family until it closed in 1918.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Patrick_Springs%2C_Virginia",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Passengers of the Danville and Western Railway, “Dick & Willie,” would pass by the Shuff depot and post office on their way to the hotel and mineral resort.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Patrick_Springs%2C_Virginia",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "vague"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "During the 32 years when the Patrick Springs post office was closed, the Shuff Post Office handled all mail for the area.",
